[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4685893694","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/120089#issuecomment-4685893694","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120089","id":4685893694,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABF00QPg","user":{"login":"BastiaanOlij","id":1945449,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDU0NDk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1945449?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij","html_url":"https://github.com/BastiaanOlij","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-06-11T23:15:20Z","updated_at":"2026-06-11T23:15:20Z","body":"This sounds like a synchronisation issue, I don't know anything about Wayland and not sure who on the XR team does.\n\nWe'll need someone with Wayland expertise to weigh in.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4685893694/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5939248727","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/120089#issuecomment-5939248727","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120089","id":5939248727,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABYgG-Vw","user":{"login":"JohanAR","id":4918549,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ5MTg1NDk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4918549?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohanAR","html_url":"https://github.com/JohanAR","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohanAR/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohanAR/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohanAR/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohanAR/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohanAR/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohanAR/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohanAR/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohanAR/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/JohanAR/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-01T19:46:20Z","updated_at":"2026-10-01T19:46:20Z","body":"This might be the same issue that I have been trying to debug today. I'm getting intermittent missed frames, SteamVR reports them as \"late start\" and they do not show up in Godot's profiler. Happens in empty VR scene, both in Godot 4.7.1 (official release) and my fork of 4.8 which I'm using for development.\n\nDuring one minute test run I got one frame spike at 23 seconds, one at 26, and then there were nothing until 55 seconds, and also a double spike at 57 seconds with only 3 frames in between (just as an example of how irregularly it happens).\n\nI have also noticed that sometimes my whole desktop/mouse stutters at the same time it happens, if I have the Godot VR app running in the background.\n\nFedora 44 KDE with Wayland\nRyzen 7 7700X 32GB DDR5\nRTX 3090 nvidia driver 610.57.04 (I'm going to try upgrading to 615 which I think is available)\nHTC Vive\nSteamVR 2.17.10 and also SteamVR [beta] 2.18.2\n\nI don't really have any Wayland expertise, but I'll continue debugging tomorrow.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5939248727/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6156899549","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/120089#issuecomment-6156899549","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120089","id":6156899549,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABbvrU3Q","user":{"login":"DanielKinsman","id":15639,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1NjM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15639?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/DanielKinsman","html_url":"https://github.com/DanielKinsman","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DanielKinsman/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DanielKinsman/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DanielKinsman/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DanielKinsman/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DanielKinsman/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DanielKinsman/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DanielKinsman/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DanielKinsman/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/DanielKinsman/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-13T22:52:13Z","updated_at":"2026-10-13T22:52:13Z","body":"Disable vsync (like you should for all VR projects) and the issue goes away.\n\nIt also happens on X11 though the hit isn't quite as bad, I wouldn't be surprised if it also happens on windows too. Either way probably not worth investigating or fixing further.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6156899549/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6204459813","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/120089#issuecomment-6204459813","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120089","id":6204459813,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABcdCLJQ","user":{"login":"BastiaanOlij","id":1945449,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5NDU0NDk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1945449?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij","html_url":"https://github.com/BastiaanOlij","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BastiaanOlij/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-15T23:31:31Z","updated_at":"2026-10-15T23:31:31Z","body":"Indeed, V-sync will limit the framerate to the slowest window. While we automatically turn V-sync off on the XR output, if additional windows are open, those will limit the whole application to the refresh rate of the monitor used.\n\nNote that we specifically advice people to turn off V-sync for this reason in the manual:\n\nhttps://docs.godotengine.org/en/stable/tutorials/xr/setting_up_xr.html#setting-up-the-xr-scene","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6204459813/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6208009194","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/120089#issuecomment-6208009194","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/120089","id":6208009194,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABcgaz6g","user":{"login":"NetroScript","id":18115780,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MTE1Nzgw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18115780?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/NetroScript","html_url":"https://github.com/NetroScript","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NetroScript/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NetroScript/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NetroScript/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NetroScript/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NetroScript/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NetroScript/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NetroScript/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NetroScript/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/NetroScript/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-10-16T04:21:29Z","updated_at":"2026-10-16T04:21:29Z","body":"Ah, this also explains \n> However, reinitializing the window (closing and opening it completely again) completely fixes the issue.\n\nThe main window is set to `DisplayServer.window_set_vsync_mode(DisplayServer.VSYNC_DISABLED)` on ready (same code as the manual you mention). However the window in the scene is created before ready is called, so it has v-sync enabled by default (as it copied the main window setting at this point in time). This then causes the lags.\nAnd toggling the visibility destroys the native window and then creates it again, which then copies the correct v-sync setting making the issue disappear. \n\nHowever I feel like the documentation could be improved, explicitly mentioning that `display/window/vsync/vsync_mode` should be set in the projects settings (or that the DisplayServer call needs to be done for every window), as the provided example code is not sufficient in edge cases like this one, as additional windows might have a different vsync mode from the main window which might not be immediately apparent. \n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/6208009194/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]